{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 214 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D14"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the furosemide injection shortage on 2020-04-07 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E68", "E60"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale East and Corvale Lakeside sites both use Accord Healthcare's NDC 16729-500-08, whose label names Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited (FEI 3004011473) as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E7", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1106244 at Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited (FEI 3008316085) ended 2019-09-06 and was classified OAI, 214 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1191818 at Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited (FEI 3004011473) ended 2022-12-02 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2023-04-05.",
      "cites": ["E14", "D21"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An import alert (66-40) was published for Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited on 2023-06-01 and again on 2023-11-14.",
      "cites": ["E16", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General also stocks Hospira's NDC 0409-6102-02, whose label names Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343) and Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited (FEI 3008316085) as registered plants.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E50", "E59"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 33 vials of 10 mg/mL, 2 mL from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East from 8.5 to 12 days on hand while leaving Corvale Lakeside with 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D39"]
    }
  ]
}
